                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "<article>\n  <h1>Super Markup Man</h1>\n  <p><strong>Markup as a platformer.</strong> You haul <code>&lt;li&gt;</code> on your back,\n  leap over <code>&lt;/ul&gt;</code>, and assemble a working page out of real tags.</p>\n  <ul>\n    <li><em>Plus:</em> nesting and closing order sink into your hands, not just your memory.</li>\n    <li><em>Plus:</em> HTML and CSS with no actual code written — the barrier to entry is zero.</li>\n    <li><em>Minus:</em> it never goes past basic markup; syntax isn't the same as layout.</li>\n  </ul>\n  <p>Verdict: <strong>8/10</strong> — a great first step, but once the credits roll it's time to open a real IDE.</p>\n</article>",
